'x_mo-definition'('x_FBbt--00000020',"&quot;The third large region of the insect body, which originally comprised twelve segments, each segment is usually formed by a dorsal tergite and a ventral sternite and carries on both sides a spiracle, sometimes, both the dorsal and the ventral plates are further subdivided to give rise to laterotergites and laterosternites. In the context of Drosophila refers to the most posterior of the three main tagmata or divisions of the body plan, after the head and the thorax.&quot; [FB:gg, ISBN:3110148986]") :- x_cid(a65b1254ebadee).
